    "placementHash": "sha256:903abb8e5487ab925e26938a2a623c3d67f4fda08c383a2073dcdaa8db00f5f0",
    "notes": "Two mapped carriageways fix the axis. The aerial fixes the arch bearings. Four sampled joins across both banks confirm the native viaduct transition at all levels. The model reconstructs the 472 m main river bridge with the 344 m arch span and two 64 m flanking spans. The rest of the Podilskyi crossing, including interchange ramps, remains native. The engineering sections inform the 35.8 m road deck, 66.1 m arch rise and lower metro level. Pier elevations and the alignment of small components are reconstructed from photos and standard terrain. The lower deck depicts the provision for two rail tracks. It does not provide metro operations or represent a service schedule."
  },
